WEBVTT

NOTE F8: single participant telling the task out of order. Jumps ahead (c3), goes back (c4), back-fills a step (c8) then corrects its position (c9), adds detail to an earlier step (c10), mentions an error late (c14), and corrects a time (c18) and a scale (c19). Synthetic.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<v Interviewer>How do you do your VAT return?</v>

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.000
<v Nadia>The goal is just to file it on time every quarter and not get a penalty.</v>

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Nadia>So I log in to the accounting software and press submit to HMRC, that's the main bit really.</v>

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Nadia>Sorry, I'm jumping ahead. First I download the bank statements for the quarter.</v>

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Nadia>Then I match the transactions in the software. The bank feed does most of it.</v>

6
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
<v Nadia>Then I check the VAT figures look sensible against last quarter.</v>

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Interviewer>How hard is the matching, on a scale of one to five?</v>

8
00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:01.000
<v Nadia>A three. Oh, and before the matching, I forgot, I chase my accountant for any invoices she's raised for me.</v>

9
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Nadia>Actually, no, I chase her before I download the statements, otherwise I forget.</v>

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Nadia>Going back to the matching: anything the feed can't match, I match by hand. There's always ten or twenty.</v>

11
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:27.000
<v Nadia>If the figures look off compared with last quarter, I go back through the matching.</v>

12
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Nadia>If they look fine, I submit.</v>

13
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:38.000
<v Nadia>HMRC accepts it and I get a confirmation reference.</v>

14
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Nadia>Oh, and on submitting: if HMRC rejects it, it's usually because the connection's expired. I reauthorise the software and submit again.</v>

15
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.000
<v Nadia>That's maybe one quarter in four. Annoying, but I'm used to it.</v>

16
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:03.000
<v Nadia>I save the confirmation reference in my records folder. Then I'm done.</v>

17
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.000
<v Interviewer>How long does it take?</v>

18
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:13.000
<v Nadia>Half a day. Well, a morning. Let's say three hours.</v>

19
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:21.000
<v Nadia>Actually, going back to the matching, I said a three. Honestly, it's a four.</v>
